WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.080
Film Courage: When you’re presented with
a script, how can you tell good writing versus

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.080
bad writing?

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.581
Let’s say there’s writing with a few more
iterations which might be excellent and then

00:00:09.581 --> 00:00:13.680
there are things where you know instinctively
this just isn’t going to work.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.600
Rhys Thomas (Director of COMRADE DETECTIVE):
Good question…A comedy (as well) is a very

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:26.520
specific thing because there are writers that
are really good at jokes and they are just

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.460
really funny people but maybe sometimes just
don’t understand story.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:36.530
So the structure…you might read something
on the surface that has really good beats

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:42.510
but as a whole it just doesn’t glue together
so the thing that I tend to look for first

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:45.480
in any script is a sense of story.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.980
Does this person sort of know the story that
they are telling and did they understand the

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:55.180
structure of things and again it’s a sort
of subtle thing that you come to see.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.730
And obviously is it a story that I like.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.989
It’s like anything.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:06.909
There are films and scripts and what have
you that are not for everybody.

00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:12.639
So I may not enjoy a script but not because
it’s not good.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.829
Maybe I’m not the person for it.

00:01:14.829 --> 00:01:21.779
But a story is a thing that I think most writers
if they can get a good handle on studying

00:01:21.779 --> 00:01:28.880
that and understanding character and motivation
and what have you that that’s the sort of

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:29.880
foundation.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.759
The joke writing and stuff I think if you
can do that as well then you’re on a good

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:34.759
track.

00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:35.759
But it’s really funny.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:38.499
It’s quite rare to see people who can kind
of straddle both things.

